{
 "what": "Io 4 Ensemble Pad with and without its vibrato (vco / mod 0.03), issue #461, on the test rig, before and after the oscillators work out their increment every 8 samples (PR #510, D-356 amended). Patches built from the card (applyPreset on Io 4, encodePatch): IO4 EP VIB is the factory preset, IO4 EP NO VIB the same with vco / mod 0.",
 "how": "tools/rig_cpu_survey.py on the two patches, --hold 4, three runs each: per phase (rest, 1, 4, 8 notes) the longest interrupt (us), the parts shed, the overload guard's mean interrupt time at each sample (us) and the late halves. budget_us 2902 = a half buffer. before: the rig's firmware at the time, PR #484's CI build (run 41349394864, FM-1_7000000), whose engine differs from main's only in the Delay's time glide, which this patch does not use. after: this branch's CI build (run 41332235221), installed by device:scenarios --install.",
 "summary": {
  "before": "with vibrato: a part dropped at 4 and at 8 notes in 3 of 3 runs (the means after the drop, 3 parts: 2150..2172 us). without vibrato: 4 notes mean 2373..2381 us (82 %), no drop.",
  "after": "with vibrato: 4 notes mean 2283..2297 us (79 %), 8 notes the same, no drop, 0 late halves, 3 of 3 runs. without vibrato: 4 notes mean 2241..2248 us (77 %), no drop. The vibrato costs about 1.5 points (the 2026-10-31 measurement: 89..91 % with it against 81..82 % without).",
  "model": "rv32 model (tools/cpu), 4 notes mean: with vibrato 79.0 % -> 74.0 %, without 73.1 % -> 72.4 %; peak with vibrato 81.2 % -> 74.3 %"
 },
